 req←CacheControl req;FormatDateTime;GetETag;HTTPDate2DDN;cache;not_modified;requested_ddn;requested_etag
⍝ Request helper for cache validation headers
⍝ Modifies the Stark/Jarvis request in-place
⍝ req: Stark request namespace :: namespace reference

 :If 0=#.DCMS.GLOBAL.⎕NC'cache'
     ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 503)('Vendor' 'DCMS')('Message' 'Cache is being built. Retry shortly.')
 :EndIf

 cache←#.DCMS.GLOBAL.cache
 FormatDateTime←#.DCMS.DT.FormatDateTime
 HTTPDate2DDN←#.DCMS.DT.HTTPDate2DDN
 'ETag'req.SetHeader cache.etag
 'Last-Modified'req.SetHeader⊃'Ddd, DD Mmm YYYY hh:mm:ss "GMT"'FormatDateTime cache.last_updated
 'Cache-Control'req.SetHeader'public, no-cache'   ⍝ Downstream caches should always validate
 'Vary'req.SetHeader'Accept-Encoding, Origin'     ⍝ Jarvis gzips payloads over a certain size

 requested_etag←req.GetHeader'If-None-Match'
 GetETag←{⍵⊆⍨¯1(⊢∧⌽)≠\'"'=⍵}   ⍝ Weak ETag supported

⍝ If-None-Match takes precedence.
 :If 0∊⍴requested_etag
     requested_ddn←HTTPDate2DDN req.GetHeader'If-Modified-Since'
     not_modified←∨/requested_ddn≥cache.last_updated   ⍝ ∨/⍬ gives 0 so invalid dates fall through to 200
 :ElseIf (,'*')≡requested_etag~' '
     not_modified←1
 :Else
     not_modified←cache.etag∊⍥GetETag requested_etag
 :EndIf

 :If not_modified
     req.Fail 304
 :EndIf
